keel-overlay-crowdsec (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First release (handbook decision 0041, first implementation, step 2).
    Depends on trixie's crowdsec 1.4.6-10 and crowdsec-firewall-bouncer
    0.0.25, as decision 0029 left the choice of a newer CrowdSec open;
    ships the overlay manifest of docs/manifest-v1.md as
    /usr/share/keel/overlays/crowdsec.yaml.
  * crowdsec.service and crowdsec-firewall-bouncer.service are left
    disabled and stopped, the simple installation's state: postinst
    disables and stops them on the first installation only, after the
    Debian packages' own postinst enabled and started them, and the preset
    20-keel-overlay-crowdsec.preset keeps systemd's first boot preset from
    enabling them again. An upgrade of any of the three packages keeps
    whatever state keel apply has set since (packages/README.md).

